Blockchain/Dev/docs/design/2026-08-11_p3-verify-list-design.md:14:- **Anchoring-side reconciler** (the load-bearing piece): anchoring owns the chain index (Blockfrost + its own anchor_store). A periodic + on-read reconciliation marks settled anchors confirmed (and failed ones failed) in anchor_store, and emits/updates the document blob (event → originate, or originate pulls on read of a non-settled blob from the DB rather than via HTTP-with-caller-auth). Result: stored state is honest for EVERY caller; the request-time chain call stops being load-bearing.
